course: dictionary
lesson: 10070
title: Thank you and thanks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Thank» is a verb. You thank someone when you tell them you are grateful for something they did or gave you. «Thank you» is the usual way to say it, and «thanks» is a shorter, friendly version.
explain: Look at this: «Gran hands Sam a present, Mum raises an eyebrow and says "What do you say?", and Sam says "Thanks, Gran".» Sam is being polite. Saying "thanks" shows he noticed the present.
explain: «Thanks to» is a different use. It means because of. «Thanks to the rain, the garden is green.» The rain is the reason the garden is green. Try swapping in "because of": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Thanking someone is not always easy. «Zara got a gift card for a game she does not even play, felt a little disappointed, thanked her uncle anyway...» Zara still said thank you, even though she felt disappointed. Good manners can mean being kind even when you feel something else.
fact: «Thank» is a verb: thank, thanks, thanked, thanking.
fact: «Thanks» is a plural noun, so say «many thanks», not «a thanks».
fact: «Thanks to» means because of.
fact: «No thanks» means you do not want something, and «thank goodness» shows relief.
fact: A thank-you note is a short letter that says thank you for a gift or a kindness.
exercise: «Thank you for the lovely present,» Sam said. What is Sam doing? | Refusing the gift | Asking for another present | *Telling Gran he is grateful | Hiding the gift
exercise: «Thanks to the rain, the garden is green.» What does thanks to mean here? | Against | *Because of | Instead of | Without
exercise: Zara felt disappointed about her gift. What did she still do? | Asked for money instead | *Thanked her uncle anyway | Refused to speak to him | Threw the gift card away
test: Which form is the past tense in «She thanked him for the book»? | thank | thanks | *thanked | thanking
test: What is a thank-you note? | *A short letter that says thank you | A joke written on a card | A list of things to buy | A invitation to a party
exam: Which sentence uses «thanks to» to mean because of? | Thanks, Gran, that is very kind. | No thanks, I am full. | *The garden is green thanks to the rain. | Thanks a lot for coming to my party.
